## Automated Hook Validation

For more efficient validation of multiple hooks, the following tool sequence can be used:

```typescript
// 1. Get list of hooks
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path 'front-end/src/hooks' -Filter 'use*.ts' | ForEach-Object { $_.Name }", false, false)

// 2. Loop through hooks and validate
// Note: This would be implemented in a script, shown here for reference
run_terminal_cmd("foreach ($hook in (Get-ChildItem -Path 'front-end/src/hooks' -Filter 'use*.ts')) { Write-Output \"Validating $($hook.Name)...\" }", false, false)

// 3. Create consolidated report
edit_file("front-end/validation-reports/hook-validation-summary.md",
          "Create hook validation summary",
          "# Hook Validation Summary\n\n## Overview\n\n| Hook | Structure | Rules Compliance | Dependency Arrays | Performance | Type Safety | Cleanup | Test Coverage | Status |\n|-----------|-----------|------------|------------|--------------|--------------|---------------|--------|--------|\n| useAuth | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Pass |\n| useForm | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ | ✅ | Partial |\n| useAPI | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | ❌ | ⚠️ | Fail |\n\n## Recommendations Summary\n\n- Fix dependency arrays in 2 hooks\n- Add cleanup functions to 3 hooks\n- Improve performance optimizations in 2 hooks\n- Enhance test coverage for 1 hook")
```

## Common Hook Anti-Patterns

Look for these common anti-patterns during validation:

1. **Missing Dependencies**:
   ```typescript
   // Bad - dependencies don't match values used in effect
   useEffect(() => {
     console.log(count);
   }, []); // Missing 'count' dependency
   ```

2. **Overusing useState**:
   ```typescript
   // Bad - should use useReducer instead
   const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);
   const [error, setError] = useState(null);
   const [data, setData] = useState(null);
   ```

3. **Not Using Cleanup Functions**:
   ```typescript
   // Bad - no cleanup function
   useEffect(() => {
     window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);
   }, [handleResize]); // Missing cleanup
   ```

4. **Expensive Calculations Without Memoization**:
   ```typescript
   // Bad - expensive calculation on every render
   const sortedItems = items.sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
   ```

5. **Hooks Inside Callbacks**:
   ```typescript
   // Bad - hook inside callback
   const handleClick = () => {
     const [count, setCount] = useState(0); // Error - hook inside callback
   };
   ```

This validation process ensures that React hooks adhere to established rules, follow best practices, and maintain high quality throughout the front-end codebase. 